From cceb5ffd69212f65b570369b93c702b584cf4103 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:23:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: soft telecine is told only in a sequence at
 30000/1001 or 30, and a film at 24 is shown at 24

2:3 pulldown carries a film at 24 pictures a second in a sequence at 30: the
detector did not look at the frame rate of the sequence, so repeated fields
that alternate in a sequence at 25 or 50 (which is no 3:2 pulldown) could be
taken for a film at 23.976, and a film at 24 in a sequence at 30 was given
23.976 too, which the times of its pictures then left every 25 s.

The picture headers now carry the frame_rate_code of the last sequence header
(PictureFlags::frameRateCode; the detector keeps it from one packet to the
next, and the demuxer gives it the rate of the container for a stream whose
packets carry no sequence header). A window is film only in a sequence at
30000/1001 (the film is at 24000/1001) or at 30 (the film is at 24), the same
for all of its pictures (FilmRateOf()). The demuxer gives the stream the rate
of that film, and the film timer of VideoPlayerVideo takes the duration of a
picture from it (CFilmTimer::SetDuration(); 1001/24000 s as before for the
other).

Tested on the host with streams whose sequence headers are set to another
frame_rate_code: 30000/1001 is film at 24000/1001, 30 film at 24/1, 25 and 50
are not film, video at 30 is not film; the 25 cases of the corpus of the
detector, 29 files read ahead as a plain read, and t_softfilm with a film at
24 in a sequence at 30 (1/24 s apart) pass. A detector without the frame rate
in its test takes the sequences at 25 and 50 for film.
